        "Elegoo ASA (OEASAB00), material values resolved from a machine export. MACHINE-SIDE VALUES ARE NOT ELEGOO'S: fan_max_speed, slow_down_layer_time, close_additional_fan_first_x_layers and the plate temperatures are Bambu's, because they describe an ENCLOSED P1P and Elegoo's export describes Elegoo's printer. 2026-09-05: taking Elegoo's whole file put part cooling at 80% (55-80% measured in a slice) against Bambu's 35, and the bed at 90 against 100; ASA then warped off the plate on two different parts, one of which has no overhang at all. filament_flow_ratio stays 1.00 (not Elegoo's 0.98) because seal-check requires 1.00-1.02 for gas-tightness. BED 105 C SET ON REQUEST 2026-09-05. NOTE: Bambu's P1 Series FAQ states the maximum heat bed temperature is 100 C (https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/p1/manual/faq, fetched 2026-09-05). 105 is above the rated maximum; see PRINTING notes for what the machine actually does with it."
